Q1. What is Route 53? 👉 Route 53 is Amazon’s DNS (Domain Name System) web service. It translates domain names (like www.example.com) into IP addresses (like 192.0.2.23) so users can access websites.
Q2. Why is it called Route 53? 👉 The name comes from port 53, the standard port used by DNS.
Q3. What are the main functions of Route 53? 👉
1. Domain registration (buy domains)
2. DNS routing (map domain → IP)
3. Health checks (monitor server health and route traffic)

